WEBVTT

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:37.230
Good morning, Ikariya.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.010
Goo... Goo... Goo...

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:42.490
Goo... Goo... Good... morn-ING!

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:50.920
Project Squid-Bot isn't going exactly as planned, is it?

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.850
Could you call it Project Doraemon, please?

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:56.420
And its name is Ikariya, not "Squid-Bot."

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.380
Not that it makes a difference, but still...

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.760
Oh, cheer up! Cheer up!

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.770
You've only had 38 failures so far, right?

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.480
It's only 37, okay?!

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.610
Kazuya, Doraemon's all well and good,

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:13.190
but isn't it time you made Shizuka-chan?

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.440
R-Right...

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:17.990
I know! The most efficient plan is to make <i>me</i> Shizuka-chan.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.070
Oh... Would you pay attention?!

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.620
Oh, sorry! Um, what did you say?

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:28.830
Um, well... The most efficient plan is, uh...

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:30.630
Rent! That's right.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:34.340
Kasumi House keeps running thanks to everyone's rent money.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.380
It needs regular payments, you know.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.410
Believe me, I know.

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:40.140
And also...

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:41.510
What, there's more?

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.150
Your neighbor, Shikishima.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.140
He hasn't paid his rent in about six months now.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.480
If you see him, let me know. See you.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:54.730
Oh, yeah!

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.230
Whoa, whoa! What's with you, Ikariya?!

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.240
Why do you always do that?!

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.320
Kazuya, if you don't forget your squid and get to school,

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.950
your Introductory Photonics exam will start without you.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.610
C'mon, don't let it get you down.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.440
Cheer up, Saotome. It's just one exam.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.570
Exactly! It's almost summer vacation.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:43.280
What are you doing, Saotome? Going home?

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.370
Home, huh?

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.320
<i>WHERE IS HE?!</i>

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:52.090
Where is that idiot who broke the holy dignity of the exam,

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:55.320
and whose snoring interfered with the exam of me,

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:58.190
the great Kotaro Nanbara, KAZUYA SAOTOME?!

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.130
Uh-oh!

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.260
It's Nanbara!

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.410
Over here, Nanbara.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:02.630
Shut up!

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.210
Oh, <i>there</i> you are.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:09.130
At... the... donut's... center...

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.390
you find a HOLE!

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.430
So, here you are, Saotome.

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:19.530
My snoring blew your concentration during the exam?

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.480
I'm really sorry about that.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.550
Just what are you talking about,

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.190
my dearest friend?!

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:29.620
Haven't we been best friends for the last nineteen years?

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.700
Why, when I think back, back in kindergarten,

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:38.210
I, with my riches, assembled an original super-deluxe super-alloy robot to impress everyone with,

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:42.420
while you, the poor kid, put together a
crappy-looking robot out of old tin cans.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:45.400
But, for some reason, some <i>bizarre</i> reason,

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.480
your junk-pile robot was the more popular one!

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:49.680
In elementary school, too! AND in middle school!

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:52.470
AND in high school!

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.220
Was that really how it was?

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:59.570
Don't you realize how annoying
that absent-mindedness of yours is?

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:00.430
Did you say something?

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.400
Oh, no! Nothing important.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.200
By the way,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.070
I hear you're working hard on Project Doraemon.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.580
Any luck with it?

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:12.240
Well, it hasn't been very successful so far.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.870
Really? Really?

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.540
Nothing but failures, day after day, huh?

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:19.630
Tough luck, old man. Tough luck.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.550
Dearest friend, don't worry!

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.720
I'm here for you, am I not?

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:05.670
I am ho-me.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:15.680
We-l-co-me ho-me, Ka-zu-ya.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.900
Oh, that's right.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.110
Nanbara Special Deluxe, huh?

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.670
I wonder what's on it?

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:27.690
I'm so glad you asked!

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:31.660
What's on that disc will make your life come up roses!

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:33.750
Yes! Your PC's performance...

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:36.790
Chance! Romance! Clearance!

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.790
Without paying anything, you can upgrade them all!

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:43.340
Recorded on it is an access password to a secret web site,

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.050
made just for a poor guy like you!

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:46.060
Wow, a secret site? Can I really have this?
made just for a poor guy like you!

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:49.590
Wow, a secret site? Can I really have this?

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:53.470
Of course! Feel free, O dearest friend of mine!

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:55.010
Thank you, Nanbara.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.340
Well, let's give it a try.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:14.000
<i>Welcome to Nanbara's Room!</i>

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:19.400
By now, the Nanbara virus in that program has infected Saotome's PC.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:24.080
Oh! Disaster! Calamity! His ultimate comeuppance! I hope...

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:28.260
<i>To enter the Nice Science Chance secret site,</i>

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:31.090
<i>please click on the address indicated.</i>

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:34.170
<i>Go on! Click-click! Click-click! Click-click! Click-click!</i>

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:40.270
<i>I will speak the password to you. It must be entered EXACTLY!</i>

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:43.600
<i>Otherwise, very bad things will happen to you!</i>

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:46.570
<i>The topic is "Emperor Nanbara's Rapid Hits!"</i>

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:51.610
<i>Hit them all if you can! Can you do it?</i>

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.610
<i>Here we go.</i>

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:54.780
<i>Three...</i>

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:55.620
<i>Two...</i>

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:56.740
<i>One...</i>

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:57.620
<i>Zero!</i>

00:07:57.850 --> 00:08:00.330
<i>...is what I'll say, and then we'll start.</i>

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:03.890
<i>Scare you? Anyway, here we go for real.</i>

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:04.460
<i>Three...</i>

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:04.470
<i>twoonezero! Number one! I have more money than anyone!</i>
<i>Three...</i>

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.910
<i>twoonezero! Number one! I have more money than anyone!</i>

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:09.540
<i>My name is Kotaro Nanbara!</i>

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:10.970
<i>I live to exterminate Kazuya Saotome,</i>

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:12.800
<i>the cause of my misfortune!</i>

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:12.810
<i>The great Nanbara is just nice little Kotaro!</i>
<i>the cause of my misfortune!</i>

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:14.760
<i>The great Nanbara is just nice little Kotaro!</i>

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.750
<i>A rich nice guy!</i>

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.680
<i>Kazuya Saotome doesn't have any money!</i>

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:20.560
<i>From here to eternity, he'll always be poor!</i>

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.390
<i>Nanbara is the greatest! Saotome is a disgrace!</i>

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.400
<i>Nanbara is distinguished! Saotome will be extinguished!</i>

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.650
<i>I am big! I am the king! I am rich!</i>

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:30.360
<i>Big! Hot! Successful!</i>

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:35.610
How much longer? How much longer?

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:37.830
<i>Since I was born, my dream has been</i>

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.780
<i>to head a huge company that runs the world!</i>

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.830
<i>But the shallow dream of my rival Saotome has been...</i>

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.080
<i>...to build Doraemon!</i>

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.000
Oh, no...

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.300
<i>So long, sucker!</i>

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.810
What the...?

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.730
<i>...has been to head a huge company that runs the world!</i>

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.640
<i>But the shallow dream of my rival Saotome has been...</i>

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:08.730
To build Doraemon! To build Doraemon!

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:13.070
Build! Build! Build! Build! Build!

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.450
What the hell?

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:26.260
Don't watch TV dressed like that.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.000
Riiight!

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:35.470
I guess this is failure number 38.

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:42.430
That's it! Now suffer, Saotome!

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.050
But what's with that ladder up there?

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:51.110
I have to know! Alien mind control rays drive me to look!

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:14.130
Damn you, Saotome! This is all your fault!

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:16.550
To build Doraemon! To build Doraemon!

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.130
It's no use! I can't stop it!

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:33.780
It finally stopped.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:36.750
Coming!

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.790
The delivery you ordered, sir.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:47.750
Please take it.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:48.870
Oh, sure.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:51.920
Your name stamp, please?

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.590
Hm? Oh, right.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.590
The stamp, the stamp... Here...

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:04.350
That's strange. Excuse me, I have my stamp, so...

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.810
Who was that? Newspaper bill collection?

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:19.320
Or maybe a surprise visit from a girlfriend to break up with you?

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.360
It was just a delivery.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.230
Well, that was my first guess.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.180
Um, Kasumi? Are you okay?

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.060
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.190
Oh... Oh.

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:50.620
I'm glad you're okay.

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:02.080
Shikishima's back!

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:12.500
Shikishima? Your rent's six months overdue!

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:15.710
I'm coming over to get it, so don't move from there, okay?

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:18.830
Uh, Kasumi?

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:21.160
Just go out into the hallway.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:25.840
I can't go dressed like this. I'll come back after I change.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.810
Kasumi! I think Shikishima's making a break for it!

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.270
He what?!

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:39.230
Why, that dirty... Damn him! He won't get away this time!

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:40.820
Oh, and Kazuya?

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:41.400
Yeah?

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:43.210
Thanks for saving me.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:55.160
It's too small in here! It's dark in here!

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.990
I can't see anything!

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:00.380
What the hell?

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:03.420
Excuse me? Can you let me out now?

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:04.320
Uh, sure!

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:09.140
Hang on a second! I'll open it right now.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:11.950
Okay? I'm opening it.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:14.980
Thank you.

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:31.400
Huh?

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.030
Are you okay?

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:39.800
Yes. Thank you.

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:42.150
I was just a little surprised, that's all.

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:54.020
I'm a cyber doll, a copyrighted product of the Cyberdyne Corporation.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:14:01.680
Customers must abide by the Terms of Use agreement in order to use a cyber doll.

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:04.820
If the customer disagrees with the Terms of Use,

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.780
he must cease use of the cyber doll and return it,

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:11.330
with all included attachments, to the Cyberdyne Corporation.

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:17.240
And what's your birthday?

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:18.710
October 18th.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:22.500
Thank you. User data has been registered.

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:26.970
Thank you for saving me before.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:30.050
My name is May. Cyber Doll May.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:35.430
Oh, right. I'm a second year electrical engineering student at Ochanomizu Industrial University.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:40.020
Student number E5523-99. Kazuya Saotome.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:42.770
You're a 99, like me!

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:44.100
Like you?

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:46.140
Yeah! One moment, please...

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:53.160
Look! This is my production number. Type G-99!

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.910
See? I'm a 99, like you are, Master Kazuya!

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:00.990
Master Kazuya, your face is getting red.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.540
Um, can I ask you something else?

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:07.630
Sure, Master Kazuya! What can I do for you?

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:10.590
Um, first of all, could you not call me master?

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:12.500
I'm not that important.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:13.990
Sir Kazuya?

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:16.520
Monsieur Kazuya?

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:17.270
Pass.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:18.810
Mr. Kazuya?

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:21.480
Look, could you just call me Kazuya?

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:22.450
Okay!

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:24.720
Kazuya.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:28.110
Kazuya?

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:30.820
Oh, sorry, sorry! Uh...

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:31.700
It's May.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:32.730
Right. Ms. May...

00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:34.750
You don't need to say "Ms." with my name.

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:37.790
Oh, sorry. Miss May?

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:40.910
You don't need "Miss," either. Just call me May.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:43.420
Okay. M-M-May...

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:44.750
Yes?!

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:48.960
May, just what <i>are</i> you? Where do you come from?

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:52.740
I'm a maid robot created by the Cyberdyne Corporation.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.840
I'm small, but I have many talents.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:16:00.390
For example!

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.740
<i>And let's turn to tomorrow's weather in the Kanagawa region.</i>

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:13.360
<i>Coming in from the south is...</i>

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.730
I can do things like that.

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:19.950
It's not very useful, is it?

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:23.590
Oh, no! I was so impressed, I couldn't say anything!

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:25.450
Really?

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.210
Really, really!

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:33.470
I'm so glad! I didn't know what I'd do if you didn't want me.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:43.310
He got away! Well, I'll get him tomorrow!

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:46.810
Mm... Delicious!

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:52.320
Incredible! Incredible, May!

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:52.330
You really think so? You really think so?
Incredible! Incredible, May!

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:54.780
You really think so? You really think so?

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:58.030
Okay, now I'll change both the channel and the volume at once!

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:06.050
May!

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:09.550
What's wrong? May! May! May!

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:13.460
Kazuya, cyber dolls like me

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:18.550
only have a low battery charge when they first arrive.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:21.680
Wh-What should I do? May?

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:28.020
Plug in the battery charge backpack that was in the box I came in...

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.250
Let's give it a try!

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:01.310
You're gonna be dead on your feet again tomorrow, Kazuya.

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:03.080
Good night.

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:10.460
All right, this looks like it'll work. All that's left...

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:16.480
Nothing there.

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:19.990
If the power plug isn't there, then it must be...

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:41.340
It-It-It's not there! Or there! Or there!

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:52.610
Not there, either. Which just leaves...

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.620
Masanori...

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:25.180
Kazuya!

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:30.440
Oh, sorry, sorry. Are you all right, May?

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:32.770
Yes! I'm fine, thank you!

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:36.230
Thank goodness. I was really worried there for a while.

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:38.570
But the way, Kazuya, what's this cord?

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:41.490
Oh? Well, about that...

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:47.270
I know it's in here. Got it!

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:50.580
May, could you turn around for a sec?

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.790
Huh? Sure.

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:53.380
Hold still.

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:54.540
Right.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.780
There we go.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.930
So, do you like it?

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:03.220
Yes! Very much!

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:05.490
I'm glad.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:15.440
I'm sorry, but your charger broke when it fell.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:17.350
I had to hack your USB port.

00:20:17.350 --> 00:20:20.030
I wasn't sure if you'd mind, but...

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:21.360
Yo!

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:24.610
Kazuya, you stayed up all night working on Ikariya again, didn't you?

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:27.620
C'mon, can't you at least give me a "yo" in return by now.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:29.490
Yo...

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:36.040
Wh-Wh-Who did this?! Who did this to my beloved car?!

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:37.130
WH-WH-WHO DID THIS?!

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.340
My name is May. Just call me May, please.

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:43.760
Could you just charge her the child's price for rent, please?

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:44.850
Could you, please?

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:46.400
Oh...

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:54.300
<i>My master, Kazuya, always blushes when he looks at me.</i>

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:55.680
<i>He must be very shy.</i>

00:20:56.610 --> 00:21:00.750
<i>I'm very small, so I have to be careful not to fall again.</i>

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:05.070
<i>I wonder if our neighbor, Kasumi, will agree to a child's rate for me.</i>

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:08.910
<i>Ikariya doesn't say much, but I hope we can be friends.</i>

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:12.000
<i>I'm glad I seem to be living in such a fun place.</i>

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.870
<i>Although Kazuya's room seems a little dusty.</i>

00:21:16.130 --> 00:21:19.250
<i>I'll clean it all up as thanks for this wonderful ribbon he gave me!</i>

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:21.320
<i>All right! I'm going to give this job my best!</i>

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:34.350
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you.

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:37.690
Please hug me as tight as you can right now!

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:40.900
Hold on tight to the warmth

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:47.450
that's sprouted inside my little heart.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:57.690
Never say "It's hopeless" and get down in the dumps!

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:59.120
Go! Go!

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:04.480
Hold on till blue skies spread inside your heart.

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:07.380
Always in the rainy days in my life!

00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:10.760
Always in the good days in my life!

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:17.770
Never hesitate! Give all you've got! Never give up!

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:22.150
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you!

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:25.570
Jumping as high as I can 'cuz I long for you!

00:22:25.570 --> 00:22:28.700
The scenery reflected in your eyes

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:32.200
is a memory I carry with me.

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:35.560
Feeling my kick though I've sworn to help you,

00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:38.910
I make mistakes when maybe I shouldn't.

00:22:38.910 --> 00:22:42.330
It may hurt me deep inside my heart,

00:22:42.330 --> 00:22:48.220
but with experience the clouds in there will clear away.

00:22:57.170 --> 00:23:01.020
Well, well, will the heat from the day's events continue to rise?!

00:23:01.020 --> 00:23:02.310
Hah! Like I care!

00:23:02.310 --> 00:23:04.320
O gentle lass, wait for me until this week has past!

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:06.990
Oh, forgive me. My name is Samba... Rumba... NANBARA!

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:08.900
From east to west, old to new, it's my pleasure to meet you!

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:11.710
"Am I Any Use At All?"
